---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="BeamCash Demo - SkanPay"
  description="BeamCash is the app-style SkanPay demo used to show seller QR setup, customer scan, and checkout approval in a concrete product flow."
  activePath="/beamcash-demo/"
>
  <section class="beamcash-hero">
    <div class="beamcash-hero-copy">
      <img class="beamcash-wordmark" src="/beamcash/beamcash-wordmark.svg" alt="BeamCash" />
      <p class="eyebrow">SkanPay demo app</p>
      <h1>BeamCash: a QR checkout demo under SkanPay</h1>
      <p class="hero-copy">
        BeamCash is an app-style demo under SkanPay. It gives merchants, banks, and payment partners a concrete way to review seller setup, customer scan, and checkout approval without treating the demo as the final gateway product.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-check-list beamcash-check-list" aria-label="BeamCash demo highlights">
        <span>Seller QR dashboard</span>
        <span>Customer checkout screen</span>
        <span>Clear demo boundary</span>
      </div>
      <div class="button-row">
        <a class="button primary" href="#walkthrough">See Walkthrough</a>
        <a class="button ghost" href="/contact/">Request Demo</a>
      </div>
      <div class="beamcash-step-strip" aria-label="BeamCash quick flow">
        <div>
          <span>Step 1</span>
          <strong>Set up seller</strong>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span>Step 2</span>
          <strong>Display QR</strong>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span>Step 3</span>
          <strong>Approve checkout</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <aside class="beamcash-hero-visual" aria-label="BeamCash demo screens">
      <div class="demo-device-board">
        <figure class="phone-shot">
          <img src="/beamcash/beamcash-seller-dashboard-mobile.png" alt="BeamCash seller dashboard with QR code and activity status" />
          <figcaption>
            <span>Seller view</span>
            QR code and readiness status.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="phone-shot">
          <img src="/beamcash/beamcash-buyer-checkout-mobile.png" alt="BeamCash buyer checkout screen with merchant profile and checkout amount" />
          <figcaption>
            <span>Customer view</span>
            Review amount and approve.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <div class="qr-callout">
          <img src="/beamcash/beamcash-logo-mark.svg" alt="" aria-hidden="true" />
          <div>
            <span>Demo boundary</span>
            <strong>Product demo only. Live processing scope is discussed separately.</strong>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Why it matters</p>
        <h2>BeamCash makes SkanPay easier to evaluate</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Instead of asking a partner to imagine QR checkout from a diagram, BeamCash shows the working surfaces people actually react to.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="beamcash-reason-grid">
      <article class="pain-card">
        <span>Merchant</span>
        <h3>The QR surface is visible</h3>
        <p>A seller can see the code, account state, and activity context in one simple dashboard.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pain-card">
        <span>Customer</span>
        <h3>The approval flow feels familiar</h3>
        <p>The customer scans, checks who they are paying, enters an amount, and confirms the action.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pain-card">
        <span>Partner</span>
        <h3>The handoff becomes specific</h3>
        <p>Gateway, wallet, redemption, and merchant status questions become easier to discuss.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section beamcash-context-band">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Built for review</p>
        <h2>Use BeamCash when the audience needs to see the flow</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        The demo is most useful when a conversation would otherwise stay abstract.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="beamcash-placement-grid">
      <article>
        <span>Merchant counter</span>
        <h3>Show what staff would see</h3>
        <p>QR readiness, activity, and checkout state can be discussed from the seller screen.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>Partner meeting</span>
        <h3>Walk through the app handoff</h3>
        <p>Wallet, bank, loyalty, and gateway roles become easier to separate.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>Investor demo</span>
        <h3>Make the product tangible</h3>
        <p>The screenshots show that the checkout experience has been designed beyond slides.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>Pilot planning</span>
        <h3>Identify integration questions</h3>
        <p>Use the demo to discuss request data, approval states, and merchant confirmation.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section beamcash-walkthrough" id="walkthrough">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Walkthrough</p>
        <h2>Three screens explain the demo</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        The flow is intentionally simple: prepare the seller, expose the QR code, then let the customer review and approve.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="beamcash-flow-board">
      <article class="beamcash-flow-card">
        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>Seller dashboard</h3>
          <p>Shows the merchant-facing control surface: code access, readiness, and recent activity.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-screen">
          <img src="/beamcash/beamcash-seller-dashboard-mobile.png" alt="BeamCash seller dashboard screen" />
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="beamcash-flow-card">
        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>Find code</h3>
          <p>Represents the scan moment, where the customer opens the payment request from a QR surface.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-screen">
          <img src="/beamcash/beamcash-find-code-mobile.png" alt="BeamCash QR code lookup screen" />
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="beamcash-flow-card">
        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>Buyer checkout</h3>
          <p>Shows the customer-facing review step before the checkout action is approved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-screen">
          <img src="/beamcash/beamcash-buyer-checkout-mobile.png" alt="BeamCash buyer checkout screen" />
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">How SkanPay uses it</p>
        <h2>A demo page for serious payment conversations</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        BeamCash is useful because it keeps discussion grounded in screens, states, and handoffs.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="beamcash-use-grid">
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Merchant review</h3>
        <p>Use the demo to show how a QR checkout prompt could appear to staff and how status should be presented.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Customer checkout review</h3>
        <p>Use the demo to test whether the customer has enough context to trust the scan and continue.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Partner integration review</h3>
        <p>Use the demo as a reference for wallet, gateway, loyalty, or redemption requirements before deeper implementation work.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section beamcash-faq-band">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
        <h2>BeamCash boundaries</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Short answers for partners reviewing the demo.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details>
        <summary>Is BeamCash the same as SkanPay?</summary>
        <p>No. SkanPay is the company and gateway invention. BeamCash is the app-style demo used to make the checkout concept visible.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Does this page claim live payment processing?</summary>
        <p>No. BeamCash is presented as a product demo for the checkout experience. Live payment-processing scope would be discussed separately.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Who is the demo for?</summary>
        <p>Merchants, banks, payment partners, wallet teams, loyalty partners, and investors who need to understand the scan-to-checkout flow quickly.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Why include BeamCash on the SkanPay website?</summary>
        <p>It shows that the team can build a realistic QR checkout experience and gives future partners something concrete to evaluate.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-band">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Next step</p>
      <h2>Use BeamCash to guide the SkanPay conversation.</h2>
      <p>Share the merchant, wallet, or partner flow you want to evaluate.</p>
    </div>
    <a class="button secondary" href="/contact/">Request a Conversation</a>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
